// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes d7-d8
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "d7.1" source="d7" target="SNOMED_CT:225597007" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source d7 SNOMED CT 225597007 = ICF chapter-1 d7 root (interpersonal interactions and
        relationships) — a navigational/category code spanning all of d710-d799. SNOMED CT has no
        equivalent activity/capacity chapter concept. The closest genuine functioning construct is
        225597007, which underlies the whole chapter but is far broader and on a different axis
        (observable vs ICF activity). Recorded as a loose related lead, not an identity. Confidence per
        rubric (related/aspect-level); consistent with d740/d750 precedent.
        """
}
mapping "d710.1" source="d710" target="SNOMED_CT:225597007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source d710 SNOMED CT 225597007 = ICF activity of engaging in basic interpersonal interactions
        (respect/warmth, appreciation, tolerance, criticism, social cues, physical contact,
        distinguishing acquaintances). Target is a genuine functioning construct that fully subsumes the
        d710 domain — every basic-interaction capacity is an aspect of the general ability to interact
        with others. Broader: target legitimately subsumes the source (target covers all interaction,
        source is the basic-interaction slice). Axis-different (observable entity vs ICF activity;
        SNOMED CT models no activity) caps confidence at low tier per rubric. Closer fit than the generic
        405074005 used for d740/d750 because d710 is the general basic-interaction block the observable
        directly models.
        """
}
